Notes and minimal follow-ups
- This is a client-only, minimal change: it guarantees nothing is sent to SS until ETIRW is typed.
- Locks remain on the SS while the client buffers. If the client process crashes (not catching signals) the lock can remain stuck — consider adding a lock timeout/expiry cleanup in SS (background sweep based on lock_time) to avoid stale locks. That change is recommended but not required to meet your stated goal.
- Existing reconnection/retry logic was preserved and reused when committing buffered writes.
- No changes required to NM or SS message formats.

If you want, I can:
- Provide the small SS-side lock-expiry thread patch (recommended).
- Convert the small lambda-like helpers in this patch to normal C functions if you prefer no C11/GCC extension usage (current patch uses local function-like variables; I'll convert to plain static helpers if you want).

